<%- include('layout-header', { activePage: 'home', title: 'Heritage Boots Storefront - Home' }) %>

<div class="card" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(240, 84, 35, 0.1), rgba(11, 15, 25, 0.7)); border-color: rgba(240, 84, 35, 0.2);">
    <h1 style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Heritage Boots Storefront Simulator</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-color);">
        This active Express.js web server mimics <strong>Salesforce Commerce Cloud (SFCC)</strong> architecture. 
        It demonstrates how backend Javascript controls storefront web pages.
    </p>
    <div style="margin-top: 1.5rem; display: flex; gap: 15px;">
        <a href="/product/8111" class="btn">View Product Detail Page</a>
        <a href="/checkout" class="btn" style="background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--primary); color: var(--primary);">Go to Checkout Form</a>
    </div>
</div>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 2rem;">
    <div class="card">
        <h2>🛠️ Topic 1: Dynamic Controllers</h2>
        <p>Endpoints (like <code>/product/:id</code>) serve as controllers. They load mock catalog data and render views dynamically. Try changing the product ID in the URL to test error limits!</p>
        <a href="/product/1234" style="color: var(--primary); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600;">Test dynamic routing error &rarr;</a>
    </div>
    
    <div class="card">
        <h2>🧩 Topic 2: Route Append & Prepend</h2>
        <p>In SFCC, we extend default behaviors by "appending" code. We simulated this using Express middlewares. Notice how the Product page dynamically appends <strong>"Promotional Banners"</strong> and logs request footprints.</p>
        <a href="/product/8111" style="color: var(--primary); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600;">Observe route decoration &rarr;</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>🛡️ Topic 3: Forms & CSRF</h2>
        <p>Secure forms must validate input and guard against Cross-Site Request Forgery. Test submitting checkout forms with and without CSRF verification tokens to see how backend routes filter attacks.</p>
        <a href="/checkout" style="color: var(--primary); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600;">Try Checkout validation &rarr;</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>📁 Topic 4: Physical Error Logs</h2>
        <p>Failing service connections (like ERP/OMS downtime) are recorded directly into server log files. You can see these logs generated live inside the project root directory under <code>logs/</code>.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-family: monospace; background: #020617; padding: 6px; border-radius: 4px;">tail -f logs/custom-errors.log</p>
    </div>
</div>

<%- include('includes/newsletter') %>

<%- include('layout-footer') %>
